  "categories": {
    "1": {
      "label": "Energy",
      "detail": "The Energy category addresses the energy consumption over a school year (including July and August!). In this category, you will find information on electricity consumption, heating, as well as gases used in chemistry laboratories."
    },
    "2": {
      "label": "Food Service",
      "detail": "In the Food service category, you need to determine the emissions related to lunch. You need to consider meals served at the school canteen, the cafeteria or at home!"
    },
    "3": {
      "label": "Travel",
      "detail": "The Travel category addresses emissions related to home-school commutes for students and staff, as well as school trips."
    },
    "4": {
      "label": "Supplies",
      "detail": "In the Supplies category, all the material bought for the school year is entered. These are mostly consumables or short-life products that will be used during the year and will have to be bought again next year."
    },
    "5": {
      "label": "Fixed Assets",
      "detail": "The Fixed assets category covers buildings/renovations and goods classified as \"long-term\" such as IT equipment, production machinery, etc. The emissions generated by the manufacture of these goods are spread over a conventionally chosen period (20 years for buildings, 5 years for IT equipment)."
    }
  },
  "subCategories": {
    "1": {
      "label": "Fuel",
      "detail": "Your school likely has one or more boilers for heating. To operate, these devices can use various types of fossil fuels (fuel oil, natural gas, etc.). Greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions generated by this equipment are released during the combustion of fuel oil or gas, for example"
    },
    "2": {
      "label": "Electricity",
      "detail": "Your school is connected to the national electricity grid. Electricity can be produced in various ways (nuclear power plants, renewable energy, fossil fuel power plants, etc.). Each production method emits greenhouse gases (GHGs) in different quantities."
    },
    "3": {
      "label": "Other gas - Advanced mode",
      "detail": "Your school probably has chemistry laboratories equipped with Bunsen burners or other devices that consume energy, contributing to greenhouse gas emissions."
    },
    "4": {
      "label": "Meals",
      "detail": "Here, you will calculate the emissions related to meals served in the school canteen, cafeteria or at home. Make sure to count the number of meals served x the number of days in the school year."
    },
    "5": {
      "label": "Vending machine",
      "detail": "In case you have a vending machine in your school, here are some of the foods and beverages you can find inside. The manager and his supplier will be able to help you find this information."
    },
    "6": {
      "label": "Food delivery",
      "detail": "Meals taken at the school canteen are brought by trucks, boats, trains or planes which generate greenhouse gases emissions. Note here the type of transport and the distances traveled. The school canteen supplier can assist you with this."
    },
    "7": {
      "label": "Transportation - students",
      "detail": "Here, you will record all home-school commutes made by students. Don’t forget: multiply your data by the number of days in the school year!"
    },
    "8": {
      "label": "Transportation - teachers and staff",
      "detail": "Here, you will record all home-school commutes made by teachers and non-educational staff. Don’t forget: multiply your data by the number of days in the school year !"
    },
    "9": {
      "label": "School Trips",
      "detail": "If your school organizes outings or trips, these must also be accounted for. Add up the distance traveled and multiply it by the number of people taking the trip. The school administrator can likely help you find this data."
    },
    "11": {
      "label": "Furnitures And Supplies",
      "detail": "Your middle school or high school buys equipment and furniture so that classes can be held and students can learn in good conditions. Here you will estimate the GHG emissions linked to the purchase of supplies other than foodstuffs (food purchases are reported in the Food service tab). Count the totality of the items purchased by the school during the school year and insert the data."
    },
    "12": {
      "label": "Chemical Supplies For Electronic",
      "detail": "Think about the materials you use in science and technology classes and labs. These products emit greenhouse gases which should be counted. You can find the quantities of materials purchased each year by consulting the invoices paid by the school. Count the totality of the items in the school and insert the data."
    },
    "13": {
      "label": "Sports Equipment",
      "detail": "Equipment is also used in physical education, and has to be replaced sometimes. Here you can report purchases of new equipment bought during the year of your inventory. Count the totality of the items in the school and insert the data."
    },
    "14": {
      "label": "Building",
      "detail": "All construction involves greenhouse gas emissions. What are the emissions of your school building or buildings? Even if the school was built long ago, it is what is known as a 'fixed asset'. To account for the building's life span, the construction emissions are spread out over the years (depreciation). Insert the number of m2 of the building of your school and of its parking lots (they can be of different kinds!)."
    },
    "15": {
      "label": "IT Equipment",
      "detail": "Do you remember our discussion of the environmental impact of smartphones? Likewise, raw materials are used to make computers and IT equipment. These are also fixed assets. The same accounting method is used to spread out the emissions over the life of the equipment (depreciation). Count the totality of the items in the school and insert the data."
    },
    "16": {
      "label": "Household waste / organic waste - Advanced mode",
      "detail": "Here, you will keep track of all household waste (including organic waste). The cook can help you gather this data."
    }
  },
